  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate 4 carries everything since rc.3. Breaking: language-tagged text is now declared by property type (string, LocalizedString, LocalizedStringCollection, LangString), and Resource.Language and the languageInvariant flag are removed. A property still declared string over tagged data compiles but reads null, so check those first. A mapped System.Uri property is refused at registration (declare it UriRef), IModelGroup.DefaultModel is removed, and Fuseki needs 5.x. New: an Oxigraph store backend; layered views that read a baseline with a pending change applied, stage commits into it, and accept or discard it; and RDFS inferencing in the in-memory store. Fixes several defects that reported success while losing data or answering wrongly: Read(update: true) replaced the graph on Fuseki and GraphDB, a bulk UpdateResources merged instead of replacing, ModelGroup.ContainsResource returned true for any blank node, and UriRef ignored its fragment on .NET 10. Reading a large resource and reading many resources are now linear rather than quadratic, and mapped collections on Virtuoso are no longer capped at a few hundred members. See CHANGELOG.md for the migration notes and known issues.",
